              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">4de6671c-8575-476c-9086-0c9d5cc3afe5</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">APPLY HEATING &amp; COOLING SETPOINTS
Heating setpoint: 20 °C (constant)
Cooling setpoint: 26 °C (constant)

Heating: Peinturier &amp; Wallom (2025) evaluate a reduced heating
setpoint of 19 °C as an energy-saving measure; 20 °C is adopted
as the base case.
  Energy &amp; Buildings, doi:10.1016/j.enbuild.2025.115971

Cooling: Algburi et al. (2025) show that raising the cooling
setpoint from 24 °C to 26 °C reduces peak cooling load from
125 to 95 W/m² and annual load from 240 to 200 kWh/m², and
eliminates the extra warm-discomfort hours.
  Results in Engineering, doi:10.1016/j.rineng.2025.105475

Assumption: setpoints are constant (24 h / 365 d), no night
setback (HB Apply Setpoint Values).</item>
                  </items>
